id: pm-lint-trap
title: "Dogfood improvement round: precise PML003, finding excerpts, scopes, lint rules and read_output"
description: "Real-data dogfood round on the ten authoring rules: invert PML003 to flag only genuinely vague criteria, add offending title/excerpt to every finding, per-rule default scopes for authoring rules, a pm lint rules command plus per-rule summary counts, real flag help text, and the SDK read_output contract on both lint commands with the 2026.10.13 host pin."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-13T12:02:03.064Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-13T14:06:08.330Z"
assignee: pi-grok
claim_principal: pi-grok
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "PML003 flags only vague placeholder criteria on the real corpus with before and after counts plus ten hand-checked samples; every finding carries the offending title and a bounded excerpt; authoring rules carry per-rule default scopes overridable through settings and --status; pm lint rules lists the rule table and the lint receipt has per-rule summary counts; every CLI flag has a real help description; both lint commands declare the SDK read_output contract on the 2026.10.13 pin and packed consumers exercise the host output flags; README, changelog and dogfood table are updated; release gates pass at unchanged thresholds"
parent: pm-lint-epic
comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-13T12:02:15.406Z",pi-agent,"Plan: invert PML003 to a vague-criteria predicate, add title/excerpt to findings, add per-rule default scopes, add a lint rules command and summary counts, write real flag help, bump the host SDK pin to 2026.10.13 and declare the read_output contract on both lint commands. Dogfood on the companion tracker and every fleet tracker copy in scratch projects."
  "2026-10-13T12:02:26.015Z",pi-agent,"Plan: invert PML003 to a vague-criteria predicate, add title/excerpt to findings, add per-rule default scopes, add a lint rules command and summary counts, write real flag help, bump the host SDK pin to 2026.10.13 and declare the read_output contract on both lint commands. Dogfood on the companion tracker and every fleet tracker copy in scratch projects."
  "2026-10-13T12:46:33.246Z",codex-agent,"Taking over the interrupted implementation as authorized. Reviewing all six findings, completing packed-host acceptance, and measuring copied real-data corpora before full npm and Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-13T12:53:05.835Z",codex-agent,"Review repairs: raise dev, peer and manifest minimum host to 2026.10.13; make excerpt required with an empty value for missing fields; remove hidden lifecycle restrictions so settings and explicit status scope overrides work. README documents output privacy, defaults and read-output shaping. FlagDefinition.description is supported by the SDK."
  "2026-10-13T13:02:50.571Z",codex-agent,"All seven behavioral mutants failed with assertion errors: original PML003 heuristic, removed scope guard, emptied excerpt, zeroed summary, generic flag help, omitted read_output declarations, and empty rule listing. Companion copied-corpus result: 937 items, 303 to 141 total findings, PML003 137 to zero. Source file inventories matched before and after. Remaining fleet corpora are being compared independently."
  "2026-10-13T13:05:06.168Z",codex-agent,"The generated changelog uses release dates and omitted the new round from the older scaffold version. Advancing this unreleased candidate to 2026.10.13 keeps package, extension manifest and README artifact examples aligned and lets the changelog script include the improvement item. No tags or release are created."
  "2026-10-13T13:06:30.272Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the changelog note: the earlier read happened before regeneration completed; the scaffold version can include this item. The candidate version is now consistently 2026.10.13 for this improvement round. Corpus artifacts used the same lint implementation before that metadata-only version alignment."
  "2026-10-13T13:12:40.146Z",codex-agent,"The inherited packed test failed because it treated item_id as the unique finding key; one item can have several rules. The replacement checks item_id plus rule and follows every page for findings and rules. A real SDK seeds four multi-finding Features after the packed CLI create smoke, reducing repeated CLI startup while preserving the same compaction scenario. Help checks normalize wrapping. Shared-host runtime warrants a one-hour packed acceptance timeout; coverage thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-13T13:36:59.687Z",codex-agent,"Full initial comparison completed across 26 copied trackers. Two remaining PML003 hits named a CI artifact and a rollback action; both were hand-checked false positives. An opt-in terminal-history probe found one short health-state false positive. Added regression cases for CI badge, preserve rollback and container healthy, and widened only the short-fragment observable vocabulary. Re-running every copied tracker with the final packed candidate. The full npm gate passed all 69 unit tests at 100/100/100/100 but its packed fixture fit the chosen budget; continuation assertions now reduce the budget until real truncation is observed."
  "2026-10-13T13:39:27.739Z",codex-agent,"Final packed-corpus comparison: 26 trackers, 5998 certified items, 2216 to 640 findings, PML003 1512 to zero. Every final finding carries a title and an excerpt bounded to 160 characters. No remaining PML003 sample can be drawn; docs/dogfood-round.md records the two initial short-fragment false positives, a terminal-history probe and ten baseline hand checks with mixed verdicts where prose still needs human review. Eight isolated behavioral mutants failed with assertion errors. SDK 2026.10.13 supports FlagDefinition.description; a fresh synthetic tracker confirmed readSettings still strips custom lint settings, so the validated public storage-helper fallback remains necessary. Linked test execution is enabled but automatic result recording is disabled by existing project policy; gate results will be summarized in comments."
  "2026-10-13T13:48:35.442Z",pi-grok,"Taking over the interrupted dogfood round after the previous agent stopped during the npm gate. Re-verifying the six findings against the uncommitted diff, then finishing gates, commit and the pull request."
  "2026-10-13T13:53:04.017Z",pi-grok,"Re-verified the six findings against the uncommitted diff and the copied-corpus receipts. 26 trackers, 5998 items, 2216 to 640 findings, PML003 1512 to 0, source inventories unchanged, packed rules artifact matches the current build. Corrected the hand-checked sample so each of the first ten baseline hits keeps its real lifecycle and a generic verdict. FlagDefinition.description is supported; readSettings still strips the custom lint section. Starting npm and bun release gates."
  "2026-10-13T13:58:17.197Z",pi-grok,"The npm release gate passed identity, typecheck, lint, duplication, docstrings, 69 unit tests at 100/100/100/100, audit and changelog check, then the packed acceptance after-hook failed removing a still-flushing package-manager cache. Cleanup now retries that race. Re-running both release gates."
  "2026-10-13T14:06:08.330Z",pi-grok,"Both release gates passed with unchanged 100/100/100/100 thresholds. npm run release:check: identity 0 violations, duplication 0/2881, 69 unit tests passed, coverage gate met, production audit 0 vulnerabilities, changelog current, packed install acceptance passed. bun run release:check: the same 69 unit tests passed, coverage gate met, packed install acceptance passed. Eight behavioral mutants had already failed with assertion errors. Item stays open for orchestrator verification."
